  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Goal**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on defining the precise parameters of this \"Gemelo Digital\" model. Specifically, I need to understand the nuances of the \"Continuo de Atenci\303\263n de la Salud Materna\" and how System Dynamics can effectively predict bottlenecks and prevent maternal mortality. I\'m focusing on the key deliverables.\n\n\n**Defining Project Scope**\n\nI\'ve scoped out the project deliverables. I\'m focusing now on building a monorepo structure with backend and frontend components. The goal is a functional Express/Node server and a React/TypeScript frontend. It requires a complete simulation engine, including causal loop/stock-flow diagrams, geospatial maps, and scenario comparisons. I\'ll need statistical validation with several tests and reporting export capabilities, plus backend Python scripts, SQL DDL migrations with PostGIS, and Docker integration. I\'ll also integrate the Gemini AI copilot and image analysis features.\n\n\n**Modeling Key Indicators**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining key indicators and flows for the \"Gemelo Digital.\" I\'m modeling the flow of pregnant women through care stages: prenatal, institutional delivery, and postpartum. Key rates like ANC attendance, referral rates, delivery rates, and mortality are central. I\'m also creating models for critical feedback loops around trust and resources. I\'ve begun to list geographic access, cost of services, and perceived quality parameters to calibrate the model, including socioeconomic factors.\n\n\n**Defining Intervention Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining specific intervention scenarios for the model. I\'ve pinpointed four key interventions for modeling across target regions: moto-ambulance for emergency referrals, the removal of facility delivery fees, traditional birth attendant (TBA) training for alarm sign recognition, and a combined package of all three. Next, I\'ll be designing a validation engine that includes Kolmogorov-Smirnov, Wilcoxon signed-rank, and Sobol global sensitivity tests, RMSE and R\302\262 against Countdown 2030, and bootstrap resampling for 95% CIs. External validation will also be included for non-calibrated districts. I also need to make sure automated reports are ready to go.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 915754244
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
