  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Monorepo Architecture**\n\nI\'m starting to define the monorepo architecture, beginning with a focus on a clean and systematic design approach. I\'ve begun reviewing the requested deliverables and functional capabilities. Currently, I\'m concentrating on the monorepo directory layout, particularly the `/backend` directory housing the Python FastAPI application.\n\n\n**Detailing Directory Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the directory structure, having moved beyond initial architectural definition. The `/backend` is fleshed out with `main.py`, models, services, and routers. I\'ve also detailed the `/database` schema and essential PostGIS and TimescaleDB configurations and seeding, as well as the `/docker` directory and compose files. Documentation will be included in the README.\n\n\n**Specifying API Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on API endpoint specifications, adding routes for simulations, validations, reports, and the Gemini AI features (curves, automated reports, and image understanding for public health). Specifically, I\'m mapping out the `/server.ts` with its complete REST API endpoints, preparing the groundwork for integration and testing. I\'m also delving into mathematical specifications for the System Dynamics 5-Stock Model, defining stocks and their respective inflows.\n\n\n**Modeling System Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now detailing the System Dynamics model equations and feedback loops. I\'ve formulated the core equations for stocks representing Women, ANC Attendees, Deliveries, Postpartum, and Complications. I\'m also capturing the dynamics of flows between them. I\'m specifically documenting the Trust Loop, illustrating how perceptions of maternal mortality feed back to impact attendance and, consequently, mortality.\n\n\n**Analyzing Feedback Loops**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the feedback loops within the system. The focus is now on how capacity constraints and delays affect outcomes. I\'ve broken down the *Resource/Capacity Congestion Loop* and *Referral Delay Loop*, quantifying the impact of delivery load and referral delays on maternal mortality. I\'m also now analyzing the impact of distance, lack of transport, and road quality to predict *Phase 2 Delay*\n\n\n**Evaluating Intervention Effectiveness**\n\nI\'m now detailing intervention effectiveness, focusing on early danger sign recognition, misoprostol distribution, and early facility escort. I\'m quantifying the benefits of each intervention, and of a combined package that achieves compounding benefits. I\'m moving toward statistical validation and testing, including the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test and the Wilcoxon signed-rank test. I also intend to perform Sobol Sensitivity Analysis and to calculate RMSE, R^2, and bootstrapping.\n\n\n**Calculating Confidence Intervals**\n\nI\'m now calculating 95% Confidence Intervals $[CI_{low}, CI_{high}]$ for Lives Saved and Cost-per-Life-Saved ($/DALY). I\'m also now planning for holdout evaluation on uncalibrated test districts, such as Karamoja, Turkana North, and Afar Zone 3 to validate my models.\n\nI\'ve also begun to clean up the file structure with the following:\n1.  `/src/types.ts`: All domain models, SD stocks, flows, parameters, district profiles, DHS data, scenario configs, statistical test schemas, report types, Gemini chat types.\n2.  `/src/data/districts.ts`: Rich empirical datasets for 25 Sub-Saharan districts across Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda, Ghana, Ethiopia (Garissa, Kilifi, Turkana, Kisumu, Kakamega, Mwanza, Kigoma, Dodoma, Arusha, Morogoro, Gulu, Arua, Jinja, Mbarara, Moroto, Northern-Tamale, Upper East-Bolgatanga, Volta-Ho, Ashanti-Kumasi, Greater Accra, Somali-Jigjiga, Afar-Semera, Oromia-Adama, Amhara-Bahir Dar, Tigray-Mekelle) with coordinates, population, DHS baseline MMR, ANC coverage, SBA ratio, travel distance, wealth quintiles Q1-Q5, Countdown 2030 indices.\n3.  `/src/services/systemDynamics.ts`: Full Runge-Kutta 4th Order.\n\n\n**Implementing Statistical Validation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the statistical validation and calibration algorithms. I\'ve integrated Runge-Kutta 4th Order for the maternal health model, and I\'ve added a file structure `/src/services/` for the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test, Wilcoxon signed-rank, Sobol global sensitivity, bootstrapping, RMSE, and R^2. I\'m also including calibration algorithms (Bayesian optimization, Nelder-Mead least squares) and statistical outputs, and API endpoints. The file structure also includes `/server.ts` for Express endpoints.\n\n\n**Constructing Front-End Components**\n\nI\'m starting the front-end now, focusing on key views within the `/src/views` directory. I\'m building `EquityView.tsx`, `ValidationView.tsx`, `ReportsView.tsx`, `AICopilotModal.tsx`, and `CodeArchitectureView.tsx`. My current focus is on the `/src/types.ts` file, and defining the data models and schema.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 898253607
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
