  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to map out the user interface components. I\'m focusing on `/src/components/` and `src/App.tsx`. The initial breakdown includes a `Navbar.tsx` which will handle the app title and a scientific subtitle, along with the country selection, all in the header.\n\n\n**Mapping App Structure**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the module navigation, building a list of key features. It\'s becoming clearer how the district selector will integrate. I\'m also now thinking about quick export options, and plan to include alert badges for potential issues. The architecture, including navigation to the codebase and the Epidemiologist AI Copilot are now taking shape. I\'m envisioning the Executive Dashboard\'s key KPIs and a dynamic chart for presenting time-series data.\n\n\n**Visualizing Data Insights**\n\nI\'m now diving into the visualization aspects. I\'m focusing on the SVG map of Sub-Saharan Africa, complete with district markers. A critical bottlenecks panel is also a priority, featuring severity indicators and recommended scenarios. I\'m actively developing live parameter tweak sliders, with an instant re-simulation feature. Furthermore, I\'m working on an interactive Causal Loop Diagram for better stock-and-flow visualization. The scenarios view is now evolving as a side-by-side comparative matrix.\n\n\n**Analyzing Intervention Impact**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific intervention scenarios and their impact. I\'m calculating lives saved with 95% confidence intervals, cost-per-life saved, and total program cost for scenarios like emergency moto-ambulance fleets and universal fee elimination. I\'m visualizing MMR reduction with a bar chart and creating a sensitivity chart that shows performance under budget constraints.\n\n\n**Validating Performance Metrics**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the validation metrics and methods. I\'m focusing on the Wilcoxon Signed-Rank test for paired district distributions, and Sobol analysis for primary parameter sensitivity. I\'m also working on generating Countdown 2030 scatter plots with regression and bootstrap resampling, along with holdout validation selectors. Moreover, I\'m working on the development of interactive reports.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 919176502
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
