    response: "I have applied the **High Density** design theme across the application:\n\n### Design & Layout Architecture\n- **Palette**: Shifted to the deep dark canvas (`#0c0e12`) paired with subtle `slate-800` structural borders, `slate-900/50` component containers, and bright `sky-400` / `cyan-400` analytical accents.\n- **High-Density Typography**: Integrated compact monospace metrics (`font-mono`) for all quantitative indicators (MMR, DALYs, test statistics, confidence intervals, and budget expenditures) with uppercase tracking badges.\n- **Compact Grid Layout**: Refactored the dashboard, causal loops, scenario comparison, equity gradient bars, epidemiological validation cards, and reporting matrices into compact, readable layouts optimized for complex data synthesis.\n\n### Maintained Core Capabilities\n- **5-Stock Continuous System Dynamics Simulation**: Real-time Runge-Kutta numerical integration across all 25 Sub-Saharan health districts.\n- **Epidemiological Validation Suite**: Kolmogorov-Smirnov test against DHS cluster GPS surveys, Wilcoxon signed-rank test across districts, Sobol global sensitivity analysis, and Countdown 2030 holdout validation.\n- **Multi-Scenario Comparison & Policy Synthesis**: Interactive simulation of single and bundled interventions (transport, financing, TBA certification, clinical quality).\n- **Automated Executive Reporting**: Publication-ready PDF and Excel workbook exports for Ministries of Health and district decision-makers."
    thinking: "**Confirming High Density Update**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the High Density design across all specified views and structural components. The linting and compilation processes for the applet were also completed without issues. This encompasses significant visual and structural changes to the application.\n\n\n"
