  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Navbar Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `Navbar.tsx` and how to ensure its responsiveness. I see multiple areas for improvement. Specifically, for screens smaller than 1024px and 640px, the header should adapt dynamically. The district selector needs to be optimized to provide a stellar user experience across all screen sizes.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Navbar UX**\n\nI\'ve been improving the mobile navbar\'s UX. I\'m experimenting with a responsive `max-w` property. Language and theme toggles are crucial. I\'m working on integrating the export buttons into a dropdown or submenu for smaller screens. I\'m also adding a mobile burger menu for accessing additional options, ensuring the main bar remains clean and uncluttered. Finally, the bottom nav gains smooth horizontal scrolling.\n\n\n**Optimizing Component Layouts**\n\nI\'m now diving into component layouts to ensure proper responsiveness. I\'m focusing on Telemetry HUD and Parameter drawers using grid layouts tailored for various screen sizes, from mobile to larger displays. The Scenario Comparison Matrix rows are also getting this treatment. Furthermore, the GeospatialMapView and CausalLoopView components require responsive handling. I\'m prioritizing the GeospatialMapView\'s container and details card, and the 5-stock diagram in CausalLoopView. Finally, modals need to adapt with full width and responsive padding.\n\n\n"
