    thinking: "**Analyzing Simulation Progress**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the `SystemDynamicsEngine.simulate` function. I\'m focusing on the delivery calculation, specifically lines 207-235. I\'m breaking down the formula for \'totalInstitutionalDeliveries\', focusing on its inputs from \'deliveryFromANC\' and \'direct\'. I\'m aiming for clarity in how these elements integrate to produce the final value.\n\n\n**Calculating Mortality Outcomes**\n\nI\'ve transitioned my focus to the mortality and natality calculations within the simulation. I\'m unpacking the logic related to home deliveries and associated complications, specifically concerning fatality rates. I\'m scrutinizing how variables like \'maternalEducationRate\', \'roadQualityIndex\', and \'qualityFactor\' influence outcomes within various delivery settings. I have a clearer picture of how \'totalHomeDeliveries\' factors into the model. Now, I\'m examining the role of `phase2Delay` and `phase3Delay` and how these interact in determining fatality rates.\n\n\n**Investigating Fatality Factors**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the interaction between emergency referral rates and institutional case fatality. I\'ve flagged a critical relationship: as `phase2Delay` drops, the `emergencyReferralRate` spikes significantly, nearly 4-5 times over! I\'m particularly interested in how this increased rate directly influences `monthlyEmergencyDeaths`. Currently, I\'m analyzing the implications of this increase on the overall mortality model.\n\n\n**Uncovering Critical Errors**\n\nI\'ve uncovered a series of critical logical errors. I see that emergency referral rates and monthly emergency deaths drastically rise. Further inspection revealed `dFacilityDelivery` and the knock-on effects. Specifically, I see `inFacilityDelivery` increasing `currentPatientLoad` and `congestionIndex`, which degrades `qualityFactor` and increases delays, leading to higher fatality rates. I\'m now also extremely concerned about double-counting complications in `totalComplicationInflow` when integrating home and facility deliveries that originated from ANC. The `complicationRisk` is added twice!\n\n\n**Identifying Double-Counting Issues**\n\nI\'ve confirmed a serious double-counting error with home-delivery complications. A death from home is reflected in `monthlyHomeDeaths`, then the complication is referred, and the same death is counted in `monthlyEmergencyDeaths`. Additionally, there\'s another overlap in `monthlyInstitutionalDeaths`! This severely skews mortality results. I\'m focusing on the integration of referral and death calculations to rectify this. I\'m also examining the MMR calculation, and evaluating that total deaths and births seem to correspond to the baseline model. I\'ve calculated the baseline deaths at 20.67 deaths per month. I\'ll see how `totalStepDeaths` plays out, evaluating its components of in-facility deliveries, complications, and emergency referrals in relation to the baseline numbers.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 957664990
    }
