    thinking: "**Designing the System Dynamics**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into designing the mathematically rigorous System Dynamics model. I\'m focusing on the 5 Stocks and their associated Differential Equations (ODEs). Currently, I\'m reviewing the required 5 stocks, including Pregnant Women ($S_1$), Women in ANC ($S_2$), and Women in Facility Delivery / Emergency ($S_3$).\n\n\n**Defining Population Dynamics**\n\nI\'ve been working on the specific conservation of population and flow equations. I\'ve defined $N_B$ as the monthly births target. Now, I\'m setting up inflow for new pregnancies, which is $1.05 \\cdot N_B$ to account for some early pregnancy loss. For stock 1, I\'m defining the gestational period and flows to ANC and delivery. I\'m focusing on the flows from pregnant women to ANC and deliveries, also breaking down the direct facility deliveries.\n\n\n**Calculating Flow Rates**\n\nI\'m now detailing the flow rates, especially how women transition between stocks. I\'m focusing on the flows out of Stock 1 (pregnant women), distinguishing between those who move to ANC ($F_{1\\to 2}$) and those delivering ($F_{1\\to deliver}$). I\'ve established that home deliveries from Stock 1 can be calculated ($F_{1\\to home}$). Also, I have formulated the ODE for $dS_1/dt$.\n\n\\\nI\'m calculating deliveries and the complication inflow. Specifically, the total deliveries are split between institutional ($D_{inst}$) and home ($D_{home}$) births. I am defining the incidence of obstetric complications ($c_{rate}$).\n\n\n**Modeling Complications & Referral**\n\nI\'m now detailing the model\'s handling of obstetric complications, specifically focusing on Stock 5. I\'ve broken down inflows from home and unmanaged acute complications. I\'ve defined outflows as emergency referrals to the facility ($F_{5\\to 3}$) and home maternal deaths ($M_{home}$), factoring in referral rates and home mortality rates. I\'m especially interested in how reducing Phase 1 and 2 delays influences the referral rate and ultimately, outcomes.\n\n\n**Refining Complication Resolution**\n\nI\'m now refining the dynamics around spontaneous resolution and community stabilization ($F_{5\\to 4}$) of complications (Stock 5). I\'m focusing on the untreated complication case-fatality rate ($\\mu_{home}$). I am also examining the flow rate calculation ($F_{5\\to 4}$), to define the impact of referral rates and home mortality on the rate of change in Stock 5 ($dS_5/dt$).\n\nI am also examining the inflows for Stock 3 (institutional deliveries). They consist of direct deliveries and emergency referrals. The total discharge rate from Stock 3 ($Exit_3$) is also defined. I am calculating intra-facility maternal deaths as well.\n\n\n**Calculating CFRs and Flows**\n\nI\'m now calculating Case Fatality Rates (CFRs) and flows for Stocks 3 and 4. I\'ve defined CFRs for normal deliveries, as well as referred emergency complications. I\'m focusing on the successful discharges from Stock 3 ($F_{3\\to 4}$) and the rate of change for $dS_3/dt$. Additionally, I\'m examining flows into Stock 4, including home births, complication resolutions, and facility discharges, along with outflows such as postpartum completion and late maternal deaths, and the rate of change for $dS_4/dt$.\n\n\n"
