  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Travel Time Impact**\n\nOkay, I\'m digging into why Kumasi and Greater Accra East experienced problems, and the Base MMR disparity. The initial focus is on the impact of travel time. I\'ve noted the existing travel times in those regions, around 0.8 and 0.6 hours, respectively. It seems the issue arose when we shifted travel time to 0.9. Now I am trying to determine what the effects of that change are, and how that can be used to improve the overall design.\n\n\n**Revising Travel Time Parameters**\n\nI\'ve discovered the travel time change actually *increased* it for some urban centers! Specifically, setting travelTimeHours to 0.9 hours for districts with less, like Accra, was counterproductive. Now I\'m revising the scenarios to *reduce* travel time significantly using `Math.min`, capping it at 0.9 hours. Additionally, I\'m setting the facility delivery fee to $0.0 and adjusting insurance and TBA influence parameters to reflect this new approach.\n\nI\'m now investigating why the baseline MMR was 710 instead of 646. I believe I have identified an issue in how institutional delivery rates were calculated in the baseline, specifically in how we\'re multiplying with `instDelivRate * 0.7`.\n\n\n"
