    thinking: "**Analyzing Accra Data**\n\nI\'ve been examining the data from Greater Accra East. The high institutional delivery (91%) and ANC1 coverage (98.5%) are striking. Travel time is already minimal at 0.7 hours. Baseline MMR is 260. Facility fees are low/insurance is high at 85%. I\'m currently looking at the `travelBenefit` component of Scenario D\'s relative benefit formula.\n\n\n**Refining Parameter Logic**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed an error: Scenario D was inappropriately reducing existing capacity in Greater Accra East. Specifically, the skilled staff ratio was being capped down to 1.8 from 4.2. That\'s unacceptable. I\'ve corrected this to prevent degrading existing advantages by ensuring interventions can\'t reduce those baselines, so that parameters use the *maximum* of baseline versus intervention values for skilled staff, blood availability, and oxytocin stock. Now, I\'m examining clinical elements.\n\n\n"
