    thinking: "**Defining Geospatial Types**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the specifics. I\'m taking a look at `src/types.ts` to solidify data structures for 3D geospatial elevation modeling. Currently, my focus is on defining types for `TerrainElevationPoint` and a more complex `HealthFacility` structure. Specifically, I am planning out the fields to include latitude, longitude, altitudeMeters, and more specialized attributes like surgicalCapacity and bloodBankReady.\n\n\n**Elaborating Terrain Models**\n\nI\'m now sketching out data models for terrain-specific features. I\'ve formulated types for `ObstetricRoute`, detailing attributes like distance, slope, travel time, and feasibility. I\'m also planning `TerrainMeshGrid` to represent elevation data with resolution, bounds, elevation, and slope matrices, and `TopographicAccessibilityKPI` to gauge terrain accessibility. Next, I\'m moving toward designing a service to generate terrain models, focusing on geographic signatures of areas like the Ethiopian Highlands.\n\n\n"
